=======================
= advent of code 2026 =
=======================

solutions to aoc 2026 in C.
no AI was used in the development of any code in this repository.

solutions
---------

each solution for day X can be found in the file `src/days/dayX.c`


building & running
------------------

each puzzle is compiled into its own binary `dayXX`,
where `XX` is the date of challenge zero padded.

to build the binaries run:

    # or make all
    $ make 

    # to build a specific binary
    $ make day00 # builds only day00


binaries will be created in `bin/` folder, so to run a solution:

    $ ./bin/day00  # will automatically read 'inputs/00.txt' from cwd
    # or read a specific file
    $ ./bin/day00 my-custom-input.txt

testing
-------

tests cases are written in `tests/main.c` for each day/part.
tests can be run using

      $ make run-tests
      # or to run tests for a specific day
      $ make run-tests DAY=X

linting
-------

the project is linted with clang-format.
once installed just run:

    $ make lint
    # or to fix issues
    $ make lint-fix

additionally license-eye is used to check license headers,
but it is installed automtically to the bin/ folder, if go
is installed on the system

